  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IMPLEMENTING THE RECOMMENDATIONS OF THE LATEST ORANG-UTAN STATE ACTION PLAN IN LOWER KINABATANGAN</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO (1) EXPAND THE MONITORING OF ORANGUTANS IN FOREST PATCHES AND WITHIN OIL PALM PLANTATIONS DATA WILL BE COLLECTED AND ANALYZED ABOUT ORANGUTAN ECOLOGY IN AGRICULTURAL MOSAIC LANDSCAPES AND HOW THEY USE REFORESTED CORRIDORS NEW INNOVATIVE APPROACHES WILL BE DESIGNED WITH NEW TECHNOLOGY TO COLLECT INFORMATION ABOUT ORANGUTAN PRESENCE AND SURVIVAL IN AN OIL PALM LANDSCAPE, SUCH AS THE USE OF PASSIVE ACOUSTIC MONITORING TECHNIQUES AND EDNA (2) ENSURE MORE EFFECTIVE LAW ENFORCEMENT, FOR EXAMPLE ASSESSMENT OF ACTUAL CROP DAMAGE BY ORANGUTANS AND PROPOSE MITIGATION TECHNIQUES, WITHIN PLANTATIONS AND INCREASE AWARENESS OF ALL STAKEHOLDERS ABOUT THE PROTECTED AND ENDANGERED STATUS OF THE ORANGUTAN MINIMIZE THE LOSS OF ORANGUTANS WITHIN PLANTATION RAISE AWARENESS FOR PEACEFUL COEXISTENCE WITH ORANGUTANS AND (3) IDENTIFY AND CREATE FOREST CORRIDORS INSIDE OIL PALM PLANTATIONS TO INCREASE NATURAL FOREST COVER AND SUSTAIN ORANGUTAN SURVIVAL IN THIS LANDSCAPE CREATE AND MAINTAIN FOREST CORRIDORS FOR ORANGUTANS AND BIODIVERSITY.</narrative>
  </description>
